## 5. Replay behavior

When `options.replay !== true`, `subscribeActionEvents(...)` delegates to the existing live subscription registry and remains backward compatible.

When replay is enabled:

```text
1. A live subscription is registered first.
2. Matching live events that arrive during retained-history readback are buffered.
3. Retained matching events are read from actionEventHistory.
4. Retained events are delivered to the listener.
5. The replay boundary is resolved from the replay cursor and requested afterSequence.
6. Buffered live events are delivered only when their sequence is greater than the replay boundary.
7. Future live events deliver normally.
```

This protects the replay/live join against obvious gaps and duplicate retained/live delivery for sequenced events.

Replay options:

```text
replay: true
  enables retained in-memory replay before live delivery continues

afterSequence
  forwards to readActionEvents(...) and also participates in replay/live dedupe boundary

limit
  forwards to readActionEvents(...) as retained replay cap
```

Existing live filters remain:

```text
actionId
runId
type
capability
```

History read filters additionally remain owned by `actionEventHistory.mjs`:

```text
sinceTimestamp
untilTimestamp
afterSequence
```

