## 10. Caveats / known risks

### Finding: Replay is not durable storage

Affected surface:

```text
future graph replay/recovery, audit timelines, process restart behavior
```

Why it matters:

```text
Replay currently reads bounded in-memory action-event history. Events still disappear on process exit/restart.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Keep docs/API language as retained in-memory replay/live-join. Design eventLogStoreBackend or durable replay separately.
```

What still needs verification:

```text
Future durable event log branch must define storage failure policy, retention policy, replay semantics, cursor semantics, and process restart behavior.
```

### Finding: Stream deltas remain excluded

Affected surface:

```text
runtime/stream, prompt streaming semantics, executeAction future streaming events, real-runtime stream behavior
```

Why it matters:

```text
action.stream.delta would touch higher-volume ordering, storage pressure, stream-shaping policy, and possibly real-runtime streaming behavior.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Keep stream-delta materialization in a separate future plan/spec branch.
```

What still needs verification:

```text
Future stream-delta branch must define payload shape, ordering, backpressure, retention, and whether deltas are live-only, stored, or both.
```

### Finding: Cross-process pub/sub remains excluded

Affected surface:

```text
future graph hosting, worker thread / child process / external service communication
```

Why it matters:

```text
Current subscription/history/replay lives inside the same Node process/heap. A separate graph worker/process/service will need a bridge or durable/event-log surface.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Keep current replay in-process only. Add cross-process event bridge or eventLogStoreBackend as a separate branch.
```

What still needs verification:

```text
Future graph/control deployment shape and whether graph runtime is in-process, sibling process, or external service.
```

### Finding: Direct-to-main upload bypassed feature-branch merge trail

Affected surface:

```text
branch audit trail, final docs status, GitHub verification notes
```

Why it matters:

```text
The code landed on main without a feature-branch merge event, so docs must explicitly record the direct upload and direct main inspection path.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Use this corrected dev note and checkpoint/bootstrap to preserve the audit trail.
```

What still needs verification:

```text
After uploading this corrected docs/dev-notes.57, perform a final cache-busted main inspection if desired.
```

